    "done_when": "A test drives watch.watch_text and watch.watch_document over a fixture record and index with a fixture price table and a fixture estimate record installed beside it (monkeypatching provider_prices.table_path to the fixture table), and asserts the pinned literal cost and the label reach both outputs, so replacing _installed_estimate() with None at either reader fails it; load_estimate declines an h outside 0..1, non-numeric or boolean, pinned by one parametrised test, and the estimated_cost docstring and the evidence fragment say so rather than claiming a clamp on read; the estimated_cost docstring states the gap as measured -- at h 0.93 against our own 0.975 the input term roughly doubles and total period cost rises about 1.6 times -- not as an order of magnitude; the fragment docs/evidence/fragments/serving-record-warehouse/srw-watch-prints-market-cost.html says the text panel prints one figure per period row and one label beneath the ledger while each JSON row carries its own cost_label; cost_by_rendering.py reads h through watch.load_estimate from the installed record /work/projects/imas_gpu/agents/third-party-cache-rate.json (h 0.9298553736359844, source_kind measured) rather than a hard-coded 0.858, the figure is regenerated and its caption names the installed record; the fragment ends with a trailing newline; gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_agent_watch_cost.py tests/test_agent_telemetry_watch.py tests/test_agent_watch_live.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at and each command's exit status is recorded as EXIT=0 or the non-zero status",
